<div class="note"><b>AI NOTE</b> &mdash; PROVISIONAL machine alignment by Codex, Tibetan-first original with its own prior source preparation; no English-first judgments read. The inflected gsum gas is the subject all three beings; gsum ga is the object all three parts, and the matrix ma negates their universal seeing. The later ma owns only n't in doesn't. Three seeing predicates resolve respectively to see at the universal claim, see under karmic force, and see under the second negation. First gnyis/two marks objects; second marks the latter two being types. Rnag khrag/pus and blood has two strictly tighter contiguous d7 members, with the glossary's reciprocal variants acknowledged. Dbang gis owns forced by as the causal expression; no bare agentive is substituted. Shes par bya ba is a complete obligatory phrase at d3, excluding supplied One. Omitted de anaphora, case/linking particles and final explanatory frame are not treated as uncertain nulls. Master noun/auto-aligned entries for zhing and gzhan are not substituted for their actual connective/other uses in this sentence. No erratum is established by identical C15:411/C16:842/C18:1125 fields or P7:21's English match with differing Tibetan punctuation and DVAGS/DWAGS.</div>
